																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13900933/seeking-greenlight-for-scp-a-k-a-the-golden-opportunity">Seeking greenlight for SCP (a.k.a The Golden Opportunity)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4841112">
									

<blockquote>
<p>There have been issues brought to me about copyright and trash. It is possible to switch the character name.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm pretty certain that just swapping out names wouldn't properly address the fact that you're still just making an overly grimdark, edgy version of Willy Wonka and his Chocolate Factory.</p>
<p>I'll be honest, I personally would recommend scrapping this. Not only does the core premise rely heavily on existing copyrighted work, there are also a lot of gratuitous horror elements added in seemingly just to follow said copyrighted work. I myself as a reader would downvote pretty immediately for this:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Even though Willy is super freaky and creepy, at first the child is not frightened. But when they end up back at the house, they suffer from major PTSD until they either die of stress, malnourishment, or suicide.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It seems incredibly tasteless to write about an entity preying exclusively on children, including abducting them in a traumatic process, <em>and</em> causing their death. Suicide and child abuse are already difficult to write tactfully; the way these plot elements have been handled currently does not convince me that the piece would be workable no matter how many edits you make to it.</p>
<p>I highly recommend that you write something else.</p>

